## ✅ SOLID Principles in the Ride-Booking Design

| Principle | How It Shows Up |
|:---|:---|
| **SRP** | `Driver` manages driver state; `TripMatcher` matches driver to request; `TripFareCalculator` computes fare; `TripStateMachine` manages the trip lifecycle — four focused classes, each with exactly one reason to change |
| **OCP** | New pricing rule → new `PricingStrategy` implementation; new matching rule → new `MatchingStrategy` implementation. `TripPricingEngine` and `MatchingService` never change |
| **LSP** | `PremiumDriver` and `EvDriver` both honour the `Driver.isAvailableFor(request)` contract — either subtype safely replaces a `Driver` reference without the caller knowing or caring |
| **ISP** | `MatchingStrategy` is a single-method interface; `PricingStrategy` is separate; `LocationService` is separate — no fat interface forces a class to implement methods it does not need |
| **DIP** | `TripRequestService` depends on `MatchingStrategy`, `PricingStrategy`, and `LocationService` abstractions injected at construction — never on `NearestDriverMatcher` or `StandardPricing` directly |

